  "rules_interpretation": "CR 118.11 preserves payment when a replacement changes the performed cost event. Supplied Yasharn prohibits nonland sacrifice costs, while the land-sacrifice controls remain legal. Casting restrictions and cost prohibitions must preserve unspent creatures and put an uncast discovered card into hand.",
  "scope": "Ten four-player supplied-state witnesses. Native paid Appraiser entry discovers Village Rites: mandatory sacrifice precedes draw, Rest in Peace replaces sacrifice and spell graveyard movement with exile, Yasharn prevents nonland cost payment, Soulless Jailer/Teferi prevent casting, Cage permits the instant, and combined blockers retain those distinctions. Two Shard Volley controls use supplied player targets with native cost payment, land destination and three-damage assertions under Yasharn, with/without Rest in Peace. Teferi loyalty, blocker board, library order and choices are supplied. No rules failure found in these ten source-only cases; full costs, casting, card and AI correctness remain unverified.",
